{"name":"Crispy Crust","hex":"#ebe0cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crispy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a crisp texture; brittle yet tender.","Denoting something is impressive or desirable; cool, awesome; fresh."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The well-baked fat on the surface of a piece of roasted meat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crispy"},{"term":"crust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A more solid, dense or hard layer on a surface or boundary.","The external, hardened layer of certain foodstuffs, including most types of bread, fried meat, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with a crust.","To form a crust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crispiness","blocks":[{"text":"Crispiness or crispness is one of the most common food texture attributes. Crispiness refers to a hard food that emits a sound upon fracturing. Foods described as crisp tend not to show signs of deformation prior to fracture. Crispiness and crunchiness are often used interchangeably, however crispiness tends to be associated with a higher pitched sound, while crunchiness is associated with lower pitched sounds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Pernil.1.jpg/330px-Pernil.1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crispiness"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"crispy":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-crispy.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d6/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-crispy.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-crispy.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d6/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vea